course: dictionary
lesson: 2235
title: Cowpox and smallpox
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from science and history, and they name things that once frightened whole countries. Cowpox is one of them. You can use the words around it to work out what it means: «In 1796 Edward Jenner used cowpox to protect people from smallpox.» Cowpox protects people, and it is linked to smallpox.
explain: Read the clues carefully. «Milkmaids who caught mild cowpox didn't get deadly smallpox.» Mild means gentle, and deadly means it can kill. So cowpox is the mild illness and smallpox is the dangerous one. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A mild disease of cows fits, and a deadly disease of people does not.
explain: Some words are built from older languages. The word vaccine comes from the Latin word for cow, and cowpox is named after cows too. When a word is new, look for a part you already know, then put your meaning back into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Cowpox is a mild disease of cows that causes sores on their udders and can pass to people, giving them a few small blisters.
fact: Smallpox was a deadly disease that people caught from other people.
fact: In 1796 Edward Jenner noticed that milkmaids who caught cowpox did not get smallpox.
fact: Jenner used material from cowpox sores to protect a boy, and this began vaccination.
fact: Smallpox was declared wiped out worldwide in 1980, thanks to vaccines.
exercise: «Milkmaids who caught mild cowpox didn't get deadly smallpox.» What is cowpox? | A type of milk that cows give | A deadly disease that killed many people | A medicine taken from a spoon | *A mild disease of cows that can give people a few small blisters
exercise: «In 1796 Edward Jenner used cowpox to protect people from smallpox.» Which word names the deadly disease that cowpox protected people from? | cows | *smallpox | cowpox | blisters
exercise: Which word comes from the Latin word for cow? | cowpox | smallpox | blisters | *vaccine
test: In 1796 Edward Jenner used material from cowpox sores to protect a boy. What did this begin? | Milking by hand | A new school for milkmaids | *Vaccination | A cure for cows
test: Smallpox was declared wiped out worldwide in which year? | 1796 | 1721 | 1600 | *1980
exam: Why did Edward Jenner's use of cowpox protect people from smallpox? | Cowpox killed the smallpox germs straight away | Cowpox made cows give more milk | Cowpox made the body grow thicker skin | *Milkmaids who caught cowpox did not get smallpox, so Jenner made a vaccine from it
